!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-template-parameter-spelled-like-an-operands-argument-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    An operand's own parameters are replaced by what the absorbing template writes; every other name it writes
    stays the operand's. `pair`'s `z: two<V, T>` fills `two`'s `M` with `mode`'s member `T`, so a parameter of
    `t3` spelled `T` would change the type of the field `t3` absorbs: a resolver error at `t3`. `pair` itself is
    valid.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
